change my plan at all!

132
00:09:13,340 --> 00:09:14,920
Now, Brunilda, attack!

133
00:09:17,880 --> 00:09:19,780
I'll weaken her with this!

134
00:09:20,040 --> 00:09:21,300
Go shrink hard!

135
00:09:22,980 --> 00:09:25,260
And now she'll weaken you!

136
00:09:31,780 --> 00:09:33,900
He lost half his life points!

137
00:09:34,180 --> 00:09:37,200
This is what I like to call payback.

138
00:09:39,220 --> 00:09:40,540
What's your problem?

139
00:09:40,780 --> 00:09:44,368
You jealous because I run a
successful company and you don't?

140
00:09:44,460 --> 00:09:45,637
Don't you play dumb.

141
00:09:45,720 --> 00:09:48,700
You know as well as I
do what this is about.

142
00:09:49,140 --> 00:09:51,900
Our families have been
rivals for generations.

143
00:09:52,460 --> 00:09:54,800
And yours always had the upper hand.

144
00:09:55,720 --> 00:09:56,700
Have you heard?

145
00:09:56,900 --> 00:09:59,637
They're about to sign an
international contract with...

146
00:09:59,720 --> 00:10:00,661
You're too late.

147
00:10:00,940 --> 00:10:02,180
They've chosen us.

148
00:10:02,800 --> 00:10:04,094
Better luck next time.

149
00:10:04,760 --> 00:10:06,400
It was humiliating.

150
00:10:08,240 --> 00:10:11,780
In the Schroeder family,
losing is not an option.

151
00:10:12,100 --> 00:10:15,077
So I decided to take
matters into my own hands.

152
00:10:15,160 --> 00:10:16,760
My goal was simple.

153
00:10:16,980 --> 00:10:21,220
Boost Schrodercorp to number one and
leave the Khyber family in ruins.

154
00:10:24,200 --> 00:10:28,612
But that proved to be a task that
neither I nor my father could accomplish.

155
00:10:28,940 --> 00:10:31,480
In fact, it drove him mad.

156
00:10:35,040 --> 00:10:37,960
With my father unable
to maintain the company,

157
00:10:38,420 --> 00:10:40,714
Schrodercorp fell under new management.

158
00:10:43,460 --> 00:10:48,797
my first act as company president
was one of controversy i

159
00:10:48,880 --> 00:10:53,597
decided to enter into the gaming
industry a business untapped

160
00:10:53,680 --> 00:10:59,357
by any other company mr siegfried
sir i'm afraid the kaiba

161
00:10:59,440 --> 00:11:02,457
corporation just made an
announcement they've converted their

162
00:11:02,540 --> 00:11:05,777
company as well kaiba corp
is now the largest full-scale

163
00:11:05,860 --> 00:11:12,757
gaming corporation that is a lie
unfortunately it was all true so

164
00:11:12,840 --> 00:11:16,457
from that moment on i devoted all
of my time to game development

165
00:11:16,540 --> 00:11:21,357
and one day it happened i
succeeded in a landmark invention

166
00:11:21,440 --> 00:11:26,097
that would revolutionize the
game of dual monsters holographic

167
00:11:26,180 --> 00:11:31,097
monster projection however
my excitement was short-lived

168
00:11:31,180 --> 00:11:36,237
somehow you managed to steal
my invention would take all the

169
00:11:36,320 --> 00:11:38,777
credit leaving me with nothing

170
00:11:38,860 --> 00:11:43,677
can that be true but i assure you

171
00:11:43,760 --> 00:11:48,017
justice will be served here
today herr kaiba your company's

172
00:11:48,100 --> 00:11:52,017
reputation is in jeopardy not to
mention the stock price of kyber

173
00:11:52,100 --> 00:11:55,917
corp is at an all-time low just
think when i defeat you here

174
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:59,720
today The world will see that
the era of Kyber Corp is over.

175
00:12:00,040 --> 00:12:02,280
Come on, you really believe that?

176
00:12:02,840 --> 00:12:03,670
Of course.

177
00:12:03,920 --> 00:12:05,897
I bet they've already turned on you.

178
00:12:05,980 --> 00:12:10,277
Now that you've finally been exposed
to the public as a thief and a fraud.

179
00:12:10,360 --> 00:12:12,040
Too bad it's not true.

180
00:12:14,600 --> 00:12:18,080
Don't blame me because you
came from a family of failures.

181
00:12:18,760 --> 00:12:21,220
I've never stolen anything in my life.

182
00:12:21,460 --> 00:12:24,657
I got where I am today from
hard work and determination.

183
00:12:24,740 --> 00:12:27,360
Two things you know nothing about!

184
00:12:27,740 --> 00:12:29,000
Now let's duel!

185
00:12:29,280 --> 00:12:32,868
And this time, when I knock you
down, maybe you'll stay down!

186
00:12:33,840 --> 00:12:34,860
My move!

187
00:12:35,280 --> 00:12:38,500
Remember, any monsters you
draw go to the graveyard!

188
00:12:38,940 --> 00:12:41,100
Well, not if I activate this card!

189
00:12:41,500 --> 00:12:42,720
Graceful Charity!

190
00:12:44,500 --> 00:12:48,720
That allows me to draw three new
cards, and then get rid of two!

191
00:12:49,300 --> 00:12:50,130
Awesome!

192
00:12:50,213 --> 00:12:52,200
He avoided Siegfried's magic card!

193
00:12:52,380 --> 00:12:54,086
That's showing him, rich boy!

194
00:12:54,740 --> 00:12:56,260
What a strange twist.

195
00:12:56,460 --> 00:12:57,989
Joey's cheering for Kaiba.

196
00:12:58,220 --> 00:13:00,380
Now I discard these two.

197
00:13:01,040 --> 00:13:01,870
What?

198
00:13:01,953 --> 00:13:04,780
Your blue eyes? But fine. Just watch.

199
00:13:04,960 --> 00:13:09,060
Next I'll remove my blue eyes and
my pitch-dark dragon from the game.

200
00:13:09,260 --> 00:13:11,500
Which allows me to summon this.

201
00:13:11,720 --> 00:13:13,420
My Chaos Emperor Dragon.

202
00:13:19,360 --> 00:13:20,360
So what?

203
00:13:20,600 --> 00:13:23,477
My enchanted sword slays
every dragon on the field.

204
00:13:23,560 --> 00:13:24,700
Not this one.

205
00:13:24,940 --> 00:13:27,777
My Chaos Dragon special
ability sends every card

206
00:13:27,860 --> 00:13:30,625
on the field and in our
hands to the graveyard.

207
00:13:31,040 --> 00:13:33,077
That's true, but there's one problem.

208
00:13:33,160 --> 00:13:36,219
You need to give up 1,000
of your life points first.

209
00:13:36,400 --> 00:13:38,117
And you can't afford that now.

210
00:13:38,200 --> 00:13:40,024
There's nothing I can't afford.

211
00:13:40,360 --> 00:13:46,480
First I play this, and next I activate
the magic card, Emergency Provisions.

212
00:13:46,860 --> 00:13:52,257
So by sending a magic or trap card to the
graveyard, I regain 1,000 life points.

213
00:13:52,340 --> 00:13:53,170
What?

214
00:13:56,500 --> 00:14:02,380
Now I give up a thousand life points to
activate my Chaos Dragon special ability!

215
00:14:19,680 --> 00:14:22,920
Once again, you're left
with nothing, Siegfried.

216
00:14:24,240 --> 00:14:25,520
Not for long.

217
00:14:26,320 --> 00:14:29,480
I activate the magic card, Port of Greed.

218
00:14:30,800 --> 00:14:35,877
That lets me draw two cards from my
deck Next I'll activate my magical

219
00:14:35,960 --> 00:14:41,860
arms card The first thing this does
is raise my life points by 1,000

220
00:14:43,740 --> 00:14:47,477
Next we have to predict how many
magic cards we think will use

221
00:14:47,560 --> 00:14:51,857
each turn And each of us will
automatically gain 500 life points for

222
00:14:51,940 --> 00:14:56,257
each card But if you use fewer than
the number you guess You lose 1

223
00:14:56,340 --> 00:15:01,740
,000 life points per card Which means one
mistake and you're through, Herr Khyber.

224
00:15:04,280 --> 00:15:06,880
Now I'll play Final Light!

225
00:15:07,440 --> 00:15:11,880
And I predict that's the only magic
card I'll activate during this turn.

226
00:15:12,180 --> 00:15:15,157
Now, for the cost of a
mere 1,000 life points,

227
00:15:15,240 --> 00:15:18,005
I'm able to summon a
monster from my graveyard.

228
00:15:18,940 --> 00:15:21,880
And I choose Valkyrie Brunhilde!

229
00:15:22,800 --> 00:15:27,357
Of course, you are also permitted to
summon a monster from your graveyard.

230
00:15:27,440 --> 00:15:29,100
So let's have it.

231
00:15:29,520 --> 00:15:32,180
Then I choose my cave dragon.

232
00:15:34,980 --> 00:15:37,240
Why, thank you, Herr Keimer.

233
00:15:37,580 --> 00:15:41,980
Your dragon gives my Valkyrie
an extra 300 attack points.

234
00:15:42,460 --> 00:15:46,520
And now, my dearest Brunhilde,
attack his cave dragon!

235
00:15:52,760 --> 00:15:56,737
Now, how many magic cards
do you think you'll use?

236
00:15:56,820 --> 00:15:59,040
You can't afford to guess wrong.

237
00:15:59,380 --> 00:16:00,340
I won't.

238
00:16:01,120 --> 00:16:04,640
I predict I'll use four
magic cards this turn.

239
00:16:04,940 --> 00:16:05,780
Four cards?

240
00:16:05,900 --> 00:16:09,017
Don't you realize you're only
holding one card in your hand?

241
00:16:09,100 --> 00:16:12,394
That's right, but that's all
about to change, Siegfried.

242
00:16:13,860 --> 00:16:16,400
No, you have to be bluffing.

243
00:16:16,860 --> 00:16:18,080
Let's find out.

244
00:16:18,800 --> 00:16:21,857
First, I activate my card of demise.

245
00:16:21,940 --> 00:16:24,917
This lets me draw till
I'm holding five cards.

246
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:28,000
And in five turns, I
discard my entire hand.

